1
00:00:00,507 --> 00:00:02,427
♪

2
00:00:04,347 --> 00:00:05,967
( ax chops )

3
00:00:09,307 --> 00:00:10,597
( ax chops )

4
00:00:15,687 --> 00:00:17,567
Boy: 47.

5
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:21,447
( boy #2 sighs )

6
00:00:21,447 --> 00:00:22,947
( ax chops )

7
00:00:24,367 --> 00:00:26,407
( ax chops )

8
00:00:26,407 --> 00:00:28,077
( boy #1 panting )

9
00:00:30,667 --> 00:00:32,667
AND 50!

10
00:00:39,547 --> 00:00:42,887
( gasps )

11
00:00:49,267 --> 00:00:50,597
Boy #2: OUT OF 50 CHOPS,

12
00:00:50,597 --> 00:00:52,977
I ONLY HEARD
THREE GOOD ONES THERE.

13
00:00:52,977 --> 00:00:56,727
SO FAR, THAT BRINGS
YOUR TOTAL TO 41.

14
00:00:58,237 --> 00:00:59,987
SORRY, EUGEO.

15
00:00:59,987 --> 00:01:03,407
LOOKS LIKE THE SIRAL WATER’S
ON YOU AGAIN.

16
00:01:03,407 --> 00:01:06,487
Eugeo: OH, WHATEVER. YOU GOT
WHAT, 43 GOOD CHOPS SO FAR?

17
00:01:06,487 --> 00:01:08,577
I’LL CATCH UP SOON.

18
00:01:08,577 --> 00:01:12,417
GO ON. IT’S YOUR TURN
AT THE AX, KIRITO.

19
00:01:12,417 --> 00:01:13,917
Kirito: YEAH, IN A SEC.

20
00:01:15,877 --> 00:01:19,007
EVERY DAY, FOR THE PAST YEAR
AND THREE MONTHS,

21
00:01:19,007 --> 00:01:22,877
WE’VE BEEN HACKIN’ AWAY
AT THIS DARN TREE.

22
00:01:22,877 --> 00:01:24,847
I CAN’T TAKE IT ANY MORE.

23
00:01:24,847 --> 00:01:27,137
Eugeo: THERE’S NO USE
COMPLAINING ABOUT IT.

24
00:01:27,137 --> 00:01:29,517
OUR CALLING’S TO CUT
THE GIGAS CEDAR DOWN,

25
00:01:29,517 --> 00:01:31,477
SO THERE’S
NO GETTING OUT OF IT.

26
00:01:31,477 --> 00:01:33,727
Kirito: YEAH, I KNOW
YOU’RE RIGHT, BUT, STILL,

27
00:01:33,727 --> 00:01:35,727
DOESN’T FEEL LIKE
WE’RE GETTING ANYWHERE.

28
00:01:39,477 --> 00:01:40,817
THAT’S ITS LIFE NOW.

29
00:01:40,817 --> 00:01:42,857
WHAT WAS IT TWO MONTHS AGO?

30
00:01:42,857 --> 00:01:44,697
Eugeo: I THINK IT WAS AT...

31
00:01:44,697 --> 00:01:47,867
235,590?

32
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:49,787
Kirito: I’M GONNA BE SICK.

33
00:01:49,787 --> 00:01:51,787
AFTER TWO MONTHS
OF CHOPPING AT IT,

34
00:01:51,787 --> 00:01:54,577
WE ONLY GOT ITS LIFE DOWN
A LOUSY 50?!

35
00:01:54,577 --> 00:01:57,287
( moans ) IT’S GONNA TAKE US
FOREVER TO CUT IT DOWN!

36
00:01:57,287 --> 00:01:59,417
( Eugeo laughs )
WHAT’D YOU EXPECT?

37
00:01:59,417 --> 00:02:00,957
THIS TREE’S AS STRONG AS STEEL.

38
00:02:00,957 --> 00:02:03,217
SIX GENERATIONS OF CARVERS

39
00:02:03,217 --> 00:02:05,757
WORKED ON IT FOR 300 YEARS
TO GET THIS FAR.

40
00:02:05,757 --> 00:02:07,717
IT’LL GET CUT DOWN...

41
00:02:07,717 --> 00:02:09,767
IN 900 YEARS OR SO.

42
00:02:09,767 --> 00:02:12,267
Kirito: OH, IS THAT ALL?

43
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:14,347
WELL...

44
00:02:14,347 --> 00:02:16,477
( both grunting )

45
00:02:17,977 --> 00:02:20,107
Eugeo: WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

46
00:02:20,107 --> 00:02:22,317
Kirito: YOU THINK
YOU’RE SUCH A SMARTY-PANTS!

47
00:02:22,317 --> 00:02:24,277
WHY DON’T YOU USE
THAT BIG BRAIN OF YOURS

48
00:02:24,277 --> 00:02:26,567
TO FIGURE OUT
HOW TO GET US OUT OF THIS JOB?

49
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:27,777
Eugeo: WOULD YOU--

50
00:02:27,777 --> 00:02:29,487
STOP IT!

51
00:02:29,487 --> 00:02:32,117
GET OFF!

52
00:02:32,117 --> 00:02:33,997
- NOW IT’S MY TURN.
- ( Kirito laughing )

53
00:02:33,997 --> 00:02:35,917
Eugeo: HOW DO YOU
LIKE THAT, HUH?!

54
00:02:35,917 --> 00:02:38,957
WANT MORE, OR DO YOU GIVE UP?

55
00:02:38,957 --> 00:02:41,417
- WHOA!
- Kirito: NOT EVEN!

56
00:02:41,417 --> 00:02:42,957
- PAYBACK TIME!
- ( Eugeo laughing )

57
00:02:42,957 --> 00:02:44,627
Kirito: NO SURRENDER!

58
00:02:44,627 --> 00:02:45,797
Eugeo: NO! STOP IT!

59
00:02:45,797 --> 00:02:47,717
Kirito: NOPE!

60
00:02:47,717 --> 00:02:49,757
Girl: I KNEW I’D FIND
YOU BOYS GOOFING OFF!

61
00:02:51,257 --> 00:02:52,467
Kirito: DANG IT.

62
00:02:53,847 --> 00:02:56,517
Eugeo: OH. H-HI, ALICE.

63
00:02:56,517 --> 00:02:58,807
Kirito: DID YOUR SACRED ARTS
CLASS LET OUT EARLY TODAY?

64
00:02:58,807 --> 00:03:00,937
’CAUSE, LIKE, YOU’RE EARLY.

65
00:03:00,937 --> 00:03:02,477
( Alice sighs )

66
00:03:02,477 --> 00:03:04,357
I’M NOT EARLY AT ALL.

67
00:03:04,357 --> 00:03:05,857
I’M RIGHT ON TIME.

68
00:03:08,117 --> 00:03:10,447
SINCE YOU HAVE
THE ENERGY TO WRESTLE,

69
00:03:10,447 --> 00:03:12,907
MAYBE I SHOULD TELL
OLD MAN GARITTA

70
00:03:12,907 --> 00:03:15,957
TO ADD SOME MORE SWINGS
TO YOUR DAILY QUOTA.

71
00:03:15,957 --> 00:03:18,327
Kirito: NO, NOT THAT!
ANYTHING BUT THAT.

72
00:03:18,327 --> 00:03:20,037
Alice: I’M JUST KIDDING.

73
00:03:20,037 --> 00:03:21,337
- ( boys sigh )
- Alice: HERE.

74
00:03:23,127 --> 00:03:24,707
IT’S TIME YOU HAD SOME LUNCH.

75
00:03:24,707 --> 00:03:26,967
( boys sigh )

76
00:03:26,967 --> 00:03:28,717
Alice: IT’S SO HOT TODAY.

77
00:03:32,597 --> 00:03:34,887
YOU BETTER EAT IT FAST
BEFORE IT SPOILS.

78
00:03:34,887 --> 00:03:36,137
Boys: OKAY!

79
00:03:38,347 --> 00:03:39,517
Eugeo: MMM!

80
00:03:39,517 --> 00:03:42,017
THE PIE SURE TASTES GOOD TODAY.

81
00:03:42,017 --> 00:03:43,777
Kirito: MM-HMM.

82
00:03:43,777 --> 00:03:46,567
ALICE, YOUR COOKING KEEPS
GETTING BETTER, FOR REAL.

83
00:03:46,567 --> 00:03:48,737
( Alice gasps )
O-OH, I DON’T KNOW.

84
00:03:48,737 --> 00:03:52,867
IT TURNED OUT OKAY, I GUESS,
BUT IT COULD HAVE BEEN BETTER.

85
00:03:52,867 --> 00:03:55,497
( boys laugh )

86
00:03:55,497 --> 00:03:58,577
Kirito: YOU KNOW WHAT?
IF ANYTHING, I WISH WE COULD

87
00:03:58,577 --> 00:04:00,917
TAKE OUR TIME EATIN’ THIS,
INSTEAD OF RUSHIN’.

88
00:04:00,917 --> 00:04:04,297
WHY DOES FOOD HAVE TO SPOIL
SO FAST WHEN IT’S HOT?

89
00:04:04,297 --> 00:04:05,667
Eugeo: HEH. ’CAUSE IT’S HOT.

90
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:06,837
Kirito: I KNOW THAT,

91
00:04:06,837 --> 00:04:08,627
BUT IN WINTER,
WE LEAVE RAW MEAT OUT,

92
00:04:08,627 --> 00:04:11,047
AND IT KEEPS FOR DAYS,
AS LONG AS IT’S SALTED.

93
00:04:11,047 --> 00:04:14,137
Eugeo: WELL, YEAH. THAT’S
’CAUSE IT’S COLD IN WINTER.

94
00:04:14,137 --> 00:04:17,057
Kirito: THAT’S RIGHT!
AND IF WE COULD KEEP FOOD COLD

95
00:04:17,057 --> 00:04:20,097
IN SUMMER, TOO,
IT WOULD LAST WAY LONGER!

96
00:04:20,097 --> 00:04:21,977
Eugeo: BUT TO MAKE IT SNOW,

97
00:04:21,977 --> 00:04:24,817
YOU’D HAVE TO USE THE FORBIDDEN
WEATHER-ALTERING ARTS TO.

98
00:04:24,817 --> 00:04:27,817
THEN AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT
FROM THE AXIOM CHURCH

99
00:04:27,817 --> 00:04:29,647
WOULD COME AND TAKE YOU AWAY.

100
00:04:29,647 --> 00:04:30,857
( Kirito sighs )

101
00:04:35,787 --> 00:04:37,867
ICE. THAT’S IT!

102
00:04:37,867 --> 00:04:39,657
- Eugeo: HUH?
- Kirito: DON’T YOU SEE?

103
00:04:39,657 --> 00:04:42,707
IF WE HAD LOTS OF ICE,
WE COULD KEEP THE FOOD COLD.

104
00:04:42,707 --> 00:04:45,587
THEN WE COULD TAKE OUR TIME
AND ENJOY ALICE’S LUNCHES!

105
00:04:45,587 --> 00:04:48,797
I SAY WE GO
HAVE OURSELVES A QUEST!

106
00:04:48,797 --> 00:04:50,677
A QUEST FOR ICE.

107
00:04:50,677 --> 00:04:52,047
Alice: HONESTLY...

108
00:04:52,047 --> 00:04:53,847
IT’S SUMMER NOW.

109
00:04:53,847 --> 00:04:56,967
WHERE WOULD YOU FIND ICE
THIS TIME OF YEAR?

110
00:04:56,967 --> 00:04:58,677
EVEN THE MARKET
AT CENTORIA’S OUT.

111
00:04:58,677 --> 00:05:00,887
Kirito: UH...

112
00:05:00,887 --> 00:05:02,397
( sighs )

113
00:05:02,397 --> 00:05:03,517
( groans )

114
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:09,067
WAIT. REMEMBER THAT STORY

115
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:11,397
ABOUT ONE OF
THE VILLAGE FOUNDERS, BERCOULI?

116
00:05:11,397 --> 00:05:13,317
- Eugeo: EH?
- Alice: WHICH STORY?

117
00:05:13,317 --> 00:05:16,987
Kirito: YOU KNOW, "BERCOULI AND
THE NORTHERN WHITE DRAGON."

118
00:05:16,987 --> 00:05:18,907
♪

119
00:05:21,367 --> 00:05:24,537
HE FOLLOWED THE RUL RIVER
ALL THE WAY TO ITS SOURCE,

120
00:05:24,537 --> 00:05:26,497
A CAVE AT THE FOOT
OF THE END MOUNTAINS.

121
00:05:26,497 --> 00:05:29,127
HE WENT IN AND
FOUND A PILE OF TREASURE

122
00:05:29,127 --> 00:05:31,717
WITH A BIG WHITE DRAGON
SLEEPING ON TOP.

123
00:05:31,717 --> 00:05:34,837
THEN HE GRABBED A SWORD
STICKING OUT OF THE TREASURE,

124
00:05:34,837 --> 00:05:36,757
AND THE DRAGON WOKE UP.

125
00:05:36,757 --> 00:05:38,517
( dragon roars )

126
00:05:38,517 --> 00:05:41,427
Kirito: THE STORY ALSO SAYS
HE SAW GIANT ICICLES

127
00:05:41,427 --> 00:05:43,897
A LITTLE WAYS
PAST THE MOUTH OF THE CAVE.

128
00:05:43,897 --> 00:05:45,147
I SAY WE GO AND GET ’EM.

129
00:05:45,147 --> 00:05:46,687
Eugeo: THAT’S CRAZY.

130
00:05:46,687 --> 00:05:48,477
Alice: THAT’S NOT A BAD IDEA.

131
00:05:48,477 --> 00:05:49,937
Eugeo: WAIT. YOU, TOO?!

132
00:05:49,937 --> 00:05:52,027
COME ON. YOU KNOW
THE LAW OF THE VILLAGE.

133
00:05:52,027 --> 00:05:53,857
- IT SAYS WE CAN’T--
- Alice: YES, I KNOW IT.

134
00:05:53,857 --> 00:05:55,117
IT SAYS KIDS AREN’T ALLOWED

135
00:05:55,117 --> 00:05:56,867
TO PLAY ANYWHERE
NEAR THE END MOUNTAINS,

136
00:05:56,867 --> 00:05:59,117
UNLESS THEY HAVE
A GROWN-UP WITH THEM, BUT...

137
00:05:59,117 --> 00:06:02,247
IF WE’RE THERE LOOKING FOR ICE,
THAT’S NOT PLAYING.

138
00:06:02,247 --> 00:06:05,627
IF OUR VILLAGE HAD ICE,
ALL THE FOOD WOULD LAST LONGER,

139
00:06:05,627 --> 00:06:07,537
AND THAT WOULD BENEFIT EVERYONE,

140
00:06:07,537 --> 00:06:09,247
SO IF WE WENT TO GET SOME,

141
00:06:09,247 --> 00:06:11,087
IT’D BE CONSIDERED WORK,
NOT PLAY.

142
00:06:11,087 --> 00:06:14,717
Kirito: MM-HMM, SHE’S RIGHT.
IT’D TOTALLY BE WORK.

143
00:06:14,717 --> 00:06:17,007
Eugeo: MAYBE, BUT WE
WOULDN’T JUST BE BREAKING

144
00:06:17,007 --> 00:06:19,097
THE VILLAGE’S LAW
BY GOING UP THERE.

145
00:06:19,097 --> 00:06:20,807
WE’D BE BREAKING
THE OTHER ONE, TOO.

146
00:06:20,807 --> 00:06:22,057
Kirito: WHAT?

147
00:06:22,057 --> 00:06:23,807
Eugeo: DON’T PLAY DUMB.

148
00:06:23,807 --> 00:06:25,437
THE TABOO INDEX.

149
00:06:25,437 --> 00:06:27,437
- ( both gasp )
- Eugeo: NO ONE’S ALLOWED

150
00:06:27,437 --> 00:06:30,607
TO GO AGAINST THAT
FOR ANY REASON.

151
00:06:30,607 --> 00:06:32,147
Alice: YOU’RE RIGHT,

152
00:06:32,147 --> 00:06:34,397
BUT HERE’S WHAT IT SAYS
ABOUT THE END MOUNTAINS.

153
00:06:34,397 --> 00:06:38,027
IN BOOK ONE,
CHAPTER THREE, VERSE 11,

154
00:06:38,027 --> 00:06:41,327
THE INDEX SAYS "NONE SHALL
CROSS THE END MOUNTAINS

155
00:06:41,327 --> 00:06:42,997
THAT SURROUND
THE HUMAN EMPIRE."

156
00:06:42,997 --> 00:06:46,497
BY "CROSS," IT MEANS
ENTERING THE DARK TERRITORY

157
00:06:46,497 --> 00:06:48,707
ON THE OTHER SIDE
OF THE END MOUNTAINS.

158
00:06:48,707 --> 00:06:51,917
IT DOESN’T SAY ANYTHING
ABOUT GOING IN THE CAVE.

159
00:06:51,917 --> 00:06:54,587
Eugeo: YEAH, BUT...

160
00:06:54,587 --> 00:06:55,587
OW!

161
00:06:55,587 --> 00:06:57,137
Kirito: THAT SETTLES IT!

162
00:06:57,137 --> 00:06:58,847
THIS WEEKEND,
WE’LL FIND THAT DRA--

163
00:06:58,847 --> 00:07:01,717
UH, I MEAN FIND THAT ICE CAVE.

164
00:07:01,717 --> 00:07:02,887
Alice: OKAY.

165
00:07:02,887 --> 00:07:04,847
LET’S MEET
IN THE MORNING AT 7:00

166
00:07:04,847 --> 00:07:05,977
BY THE NORTH GATE.

167
00:07:05,977 --> 00:07:06,977
Kirito: YOU GOT IT!

168
00:07:06,977 --> 00:07:08,097
AND DON’T OVERSLEEP.

169
00:07:08,097 --> 00:07:08,857
Alice: OH, PLEASE!

170
00:07:08,857 --> 00:07:10,607
♪

171
00:07:10,607 --> 00:07:12,027
( Alice humming )

172
00:07:16,817 --> 00:07:19,157
Kirito: MAKING US
CARRY EVERYTHING.

173
00:07:19,157 --> 00:07:21,657
WHO DOES SHE THINK WE ARE,
HER SERVANTS?

174
00:07:21,657 --> 00:07:23,077
Eugeo: STOP COMPLAINING.

175
00:07:23,077 --> 00:07:25,827
BE HAPPY WE CAN STILL
GO AND DO STUFF WITH HER.

176
00:07:25,827 --> 00:07:28,787
- THAT’LL END SOON.
- Kirito: WHY?

177
00:07:28,787 --> 00:07:30,997
Eugeo: SHE’S THE VILLAGE ELDER’S
DAUGHTER, THAT’S WHY.

178
00:07:30,997 --> 00:07:34,297
SHE HAS TO LEARN ALL THAT STUFF
A LADY’S SUPPOSED TO KNOW,

179
00:07:34,297 --> 00:07:35,627
LIKE MANNERS AND ETIQUETTE.

180
00:07:35,627 --> 00:07:37,877
Kirito: YEAH,
AND SINCE SHE WASN’T

181
00:07:37,877 --> 00:07:39,887
GIVEN A CALLING LIKE WE WERE,

182
00:07:39,887 --> 00:07:42,387
SHE HAS TO STUDY ALL THOSE
SACRED ART SKILLS, TOO.

183
00:07:42,387 --> 00:07:45,057
Eugeo: SHE’S GOING TO BE
A ROLE MODEL FOR THE VILLAGERS.

184
00:07:45,057 --> 00:07:47,437
THAT MEANS NO MORE PLAYING
WITH US BOYS ANY MORE.

185
00:07:47,437 --> 00:07:49,937
Alice: ALL RIGHT,
WHAT ARE THE TWO OF YOU

186
00:07:49,937 --> 00:07:51,307
WHISPERING ABOUT BACK THERE?

187
00:07:51,307 --> 00:07:54,067
Kirito: HUH? UM, NOTHING! RIGHT?

188
00:07:54,067 --> 00:07:55,487
Eugeo: R-RIGHT.

189
00:07:55,487 --> 00:07:57,357
WE WERE JUST SAYING
HOW WE’D GET IN TROUBLE

190
00:07:57,357 --> 00:08:00,027
IF WE DON’T MAKE IT BACK
BEFORE THE EVENING BELL.

191
00:08:00,027 --> 00:08:01,027
Alice: OH.

192
00:08:01,027 --> 00:08:02,987
GOOD POINT.

193
00:08:02,987 --> 00:08:05,037
THEN KEEP AN EYE ON SOLUS,

194
00:08:05,037 --> 00:08:07,247
AND WHEN IT’S IN THE MIDDLE
OF THE SKY, WE’LL HEAD BACK.

195
00:08:07,247 --> 00:08:10,577
COME ON, GUYS.
BACK TO OUR QUEST!

196
00:08:10,577 --> 00:08:11,577
Boys: UH...

197
00:08:11,577 --> 00:08:12,787
( both chuckle )

198
00:08:19,877 --> 00:08:22,467
Kirito: WE’RE PRETTY FAR
FROM THE VILLAGE NOW.

199
00:08:22,467 --> 00:08:25,007
DID YOU KNOW,
BACK IN THE OLDEN DAYS,

200
00:08:25,007 --> 00:08:27,427
BACK WHEN RULID
WAS FIRST FOUNDED,

201
00:08:27,427 --> 00:08:30,517
GOBLINS AND ORCS CAME DOWN
FROM THE DARK TERRITORY,

202
00:08:30,517 --> 00:08:33,857
RAIDED THE VILLAGE, AND STOLE
A BUNCH OF SHEEP AND KIDS?

203
00:08:33,857 --> 00:08:36,107
Alice: LISTEN, IF YOU’RE
TRYING TO SCARE ME, STOP IT.

204
00:08:36,107 --> 00:08:37,897
I KNOW THE STORY.

205
00:08:37,897 --> 00:08:40,027
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT
CAME FROM CENTORIA

206
00:08:40,027 --> 00:08:42,367
AND CHASED THEM ALL AWAY
IN THE END.

207
00:08:42,367 --> 00:08:44,577
Kirito: THAT’S RIGHT,
AND, EVER SINCE,

208
00:08:44,577 --> 00:08:47,537
ON CLEAR DAYS, YOU’LL SEE
A SILVER DRAGON KNIGHT

209
00:08:47,537 --> 00:08:49,907
SOARING ABOVE THE END MOUNTAINS,
EVER VIGILANT!

210
00:08:51,997 --> 00:08:53,957
( both gasp )

211
00:08:53,957 --> 00:08:55,417
Kirito: HMM?

212
00:09:00,427 --> 00:09:02,837
Alice: WE ALL SAW THAT, RIGHT?

213
00:09:20,197 --> 00:09:21,237
( gasps )

214
00:09:21,237 --> 00:09:23,737
IT’S THE CAVE.

215
00:09:23,737 --> 00:09:25,987
WE REACHED THE END MOUNTAINS.

216
00:09:34,287 --> 00:09:37,127
LET’S GO IN. IT’S WHY
WE CAME HERE, AFTER ALL.

217
00:09:39,207 --> 00:09:41,087
SYSTEM CALL.

218
00:09:41,087 --> 00:09:43,297
GENERATE LUMINOUS ELEMENT.

219
00:09:43,297 --> 00:09:44,967
ADHERE.

220
00:09:44,967 --> 00:09:46,547
( boys gasp )

221
00:09:47,927 --> 00:09:49,807
♪

222
00:09:51,137 --> 00:09:52,807
( footsteps echoing )

223
00:09:54,977 --> 00:09:58,357
Eugeo: WELL, I DON’T SEE
ANY ICICLES YET.

224
00:09:58,357 --> 00:10:00,857
DIDN’T YOU SAY THEY WERE
SUPPOSED TO BE A LITTLE WAYS IN?

225
00:10:00,857 --> 00:10:02,487
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW. DID I?

226
00:10:02,487 --> 00:10:03,567
- Eugeo: YOU DID!
- Kirito: HUH.

227
00:10:07,407 --> 00:10:08,407
( gasps )

228
00:10:08,407 --> 00:10:09,787
Alice: EUGEO.

229
00:10:09,787 --> 00:10:11,407
Eugeo: YEAH?

230
00:10:11,407 --> 00:10:13,617
Alice: COULD YOU PLEASE
BRING THAT LIGHT OVER HERE?

231
00:10:18,837 --> 00:10:20,127
Eugeo: WHOA!

232
00:10:21,337 --> 00:10:22,337
Alice: SEE THAT?

233
00:10:22,337 --> 00:10:23,837
IT’S COLDER NOW.

234
00:10:23,837 --> 00:10:25,587
Kirito: YOU’RE RIGHT.
IT TOTALLY IS.

235
00:10:25,587 --> 00:10:28,297
FOR A SECOND THERE, I THOUGHT I
WAS COMING DOWN WITH SOMETHING.

236
00:10:28,297 --> 00:10:30,387
Alice: IT’S KIND OF NEAT
HOW IT’S WINTER IN HERE,

237
00:10:30,387 --> 00:10:32,097
BUT SUMMER OUTSIDE.

238
00:10:32,097 --> 00:10:34,477
I BET WE’LL FIND SOME ICE
FURTHER IN.

239
00:10:34,477 --> 00:10:37,767
Eugeo: YEAH. HOPEFULLY
NOT TOO MUCH FURTHER IN.

240
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:39,227
Alice: WHAT ARE WE GOING TO DO

241
00:10:39,227 --> 00:10:41,727
IF WE HAPPEN TO COME ACROSS
A WHITE DRAGON?

242
00:10:41,727 --> 00:10:44,197
Eugeo: WE’LL RUN AWAY
AS FAST AS WE CAN.

243
00:10:44,197 --> 00:10:45,607
Kirito: AH, QUIT WORRYIN’.

244
00:10:45,607 --> 00:10:47,867
I SERIOUSLY DOUBT
IT’S GONNA MIND

245
00:10:47,867 --> 00:10:50,447
IF WE TAKE A COUPLE ICICLES.

246
00:10:50,447 --> 00:10:54,657
HMM. IT’D BE NEAT IF WE COULD
GRAB ONE OF ITS SCALES, THOUGH.

247
00:10:54,657 --> 00:10:57,127
Eugeo: NO.
WE ARE NOT DOING THAT.

248
00:10:57,127 --> 00:10:58,707
Kirito: WHY NOT?

249
00:10:58,707 --> 00:11:02,047
HOW ELSE ARE WE GONNA PROVE
WE SAW A REAL, LIVE DRAGON?

250
00:11:02,047 --> 00:11:03,047
( crackle )

251
00:11:03,047 --> 00:11:04,757
- ( boys gasp )
- Alice: EH?

252
00:11:06,177 --> 00:11:08,757
Eugeo: LOOK! IT’S ICE!

253
00:11:08,757 --> 00:11:11,347
IT’S TRUE!
THERE’S ICE IN HERE!

254
00:11:11,347 --> 00:11:14,807
Kirito: AND I BET YOU GUYS
THERE’S EVEN MORE UP AHEAD!

255
00:11:14,807 --> 00:11:16,307
♪

256
00:11:22,437 --> 00:11:23,737
Eugeo: SEE THAT?!

257
00:11:31,327 --> 00:11:32,867
( gasps )

258
00:11:40,787 --> 00:11:42,747
( Kirito gasps )

259
00:11:45,207 --> 00:11:46,797
Alice: WITH THIS MUCH ICE,

260
00:11:46,797 --> 00:11:49,047
WE CAN KEEP ALL THE FOOD
IN THE VILLAGE COLD.

261
00:11:49,047 --> 00:11:50,507
Kirito: HECK,
WITH THIS MUCH ICE,

262
00:11:50,507 --> 00:11:53,097
YOU CAN KEEP THE WHOLE
DANG VILLAGE COLD FOREVER.

263
00:11:55,097 --> 00:11:56,307
Eugeo: JEEZ, WOULD YOU WATCH
WHERE YOU’RE GOING?

264
00:11:56,307 --> 00:11:57,807
Kirito: EUGEO, LOOK.

265
00:11:57,807 --> 00:11:58,807
Eugeo: EH?

266
00:11:58,807 --> 00:11:59,807
( gasps )

267
00:11:59,807 --> 00:12:01,187
Kirito: THERE IT IS.

268
00:12:01,187 --> 00:12:02,227
( Alice gasps )

269
00:12:02,227 --> 00:12:04,187
Kirito: WHOA.

270
00:12:07,897 --> 00:12:10,987
Eugeo: THE DRAGON. NO WAY.

271
00:12:10,987 --> 00:12:12,367
Alice: HOW DID IT DIE?

272
00:12:15,787 --> 00:12:19,497
Kirito: LOOK. ITS CLAW’S
ALL COVERED IN GOUGES,

273
00:12:19,497 --> 00:12:22,087
AND THEN IT WAS
CHOPPED CLEAN OFF.

274
00:12:22,087 --> 00:12:24,127
Alice: THEN IT MUST HAVE
FOUGHT WITH SOMETHING.

275
00:12:24,127 --> 00:12:26,337
BUT I DON’T KNOW OF ANYTHING
THAT COULD KILL A DRAGON.

276
00:12:28,167 --> 00:12:30,587
Kirito: A SWORD
MADE THESE MARKS.

277
00:12:30,587 --> 00:12:33,297
IT’S OBVIOUS WHAT KILLED IT,
A HUMAN.

278
00:12:33,297 --> 00:12:35,137
( Eugeo gasps )

279
00:12:35,137 --> 00:12:37,307
Alice: BUT WHO?

280
00:12:37,307 --> 00:12:40,017
IF A SWORD-MASTER LIKE BERCOULI
COULDN’T FIGHT IT,

281
00:12:40,017 --> 00:12:42,187
WHO’D BE STRONG ENOUGH
TO KILL IT?

282
00:12:42,187 --> 00:12:43,397
( gasps )

283
00:12:43,397 --> 00:12:45,777
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT.

284
00:12:45,777 --> 00:12:50,107
BUT WHY? THE WHITE DRAGONS
PROTECT OUR REALM.

285
00:12:50,107 --> 00:12:53,237
WHY WOULD AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT
FROM THE AXIOM CHURCH KILL ONE?

286
00:12:53,237 --> 00:12:55,327
Eugeo: WAIT A SECOND.

287
00:12:55,327 --> 00:12:58,117
MAYBE THE DARK TERRITORY
HAS STRONG KNIGHTS, TOO,

288
00:12:58,117 --> 00:12:59,997
AND ONE OF THEM KILLED IT.

289
00:12:59,997 --> 00:13:02,497
IF THAT’S TRUE,
THEN THE ARMIES OF DARKNESS

290
00:13:02,497 --> 00:13:05,287
COULD EASILY CROSS
THE END MOUNTAINS AND ATTACK US.

291
00:13:05,287 --> 00:13:06,297
( gasps )

292
00:13:06,297 --> 00:13:07,507
- ( Kirito grunting )
- Eugeo: WAIT!

293
00:13:07,507 --> 00:13:09,127
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?!

294
00:13:09,127 --> 00:13:11,297
Kirito: THIS IS HEAVIER
THAN IT LOOKS.

295
00:13:11,297 --> 00:13:12,297
( grunting )

296
00:13:12,297 --> 00:13:13,387
( Alice gasps )

297
00:13:13,387 --> 00:13:15,007
IS THAT THE SWORD?

298
00:13:15,007 --> 00:13:19,017
Kirito: YEAH, THE SAME ONE
BERCOULI TRIED TO STEAL,

299
00:13:19,017 --> 00:13:22,097
THE BLUE ROSE SWORD.

300
00:13:23,937 --> 00:13:25,147
( sighs )

301
00:13:25,147 --> 00:13:27,687
( grunting )

302
00:13:30,067 --> 00:13:34,277
IT’S TOO HEAVY.
I CAN’T LIFT IT.

303
00:13:34,277 --> 00:13:38,617
EVEN WITH EUGEO’S HELP, WE’D
NEVER CARRY THIS BACK TO TOWN.

304
00:13:38,617 --> 00:13:41,577
THERE’S A BUNCH OF OTHER
TREASURE WE COULD TAKE, THOUGH.

305
00:13:41,577 --> 00:13:44,167
Alice: MM-HMM.

306
00:13:44,167 --> 00:13:46,787
BUT SOMETHING ABOUT THAT
DOESN’T FEEL RIGHT.

307
00:13:46,787 --> 00:13:50,007
IT WOULD BE LIKE GRAVE ROBBING.

308
00:13:50,007 --> 00:13:52,677
Kirito: YEAH,
I GUESS YOU’RE RIGHT.

309
00:13:52,677 --> 00:13:55,677
WE’LL JUST TAKE ICE.
THE DRAGON WON’T MIND THAT.

310
00:13:57,137 --> 00:13:58,767
Alice: HOW PRETTY!

311
00:13:58,767 --> 00:14:01,477
IT’S A SHAME IT’S
JUST GOING TO END UP MELTING.

312
00:14:01,477 --> 00:14:03,227
Kirito: I COULDN’T CARE LESS,

313
00:14:03,227 --> 00:14:05,897
AS LONG AS IT
MAKES OUR MEALS LAST LONGER.

314
00:14:05,897 --> 00:14:08,017
Alice: NOT JUST OUR MEALS,
EVERYONE’S.

315
00:14:08,017 --> 00:14:09,857
Eugeo: WE SHOULD START
HEADING BACK NOW,

316
00:14:09,857 --> 00:14:12,487
OR ELSE WE WON’T MAKE IT
TO TOWN BEFORE DARK.

317
00:14:12,487 --> 00:14:13,147
Alice: YOU’RE RIGHT.

318
00:14:14,947 --> 00:14:17,407
( ice crackling )

319
00:14:17,407 --> 00:14:19,197
WAIT.

320
00:14:19,197 --> 00:14:23,037
DO YOU REMEMBER
WHICH TUNNEL WE CAME IN FROM?

321
00:14:26,327 --> 00:14:29,207
WE’VE BEEN WALKING A LONG TIME.

322
00:14:29,207 --> 00:14:32,297
IS THIS THE RIGHT TUNNEL,
OR WAS IT THE OTHER?

323
00:14:32,297 --> 00:14:34,177
Kirito: SERIOUSLY?

324
00:14:34,177 --> 00:14:36,507
WE PICKED THIS ONE
’CAUSE YOU SAID WE SHOULD.

325
00:14:36,507 --> 00:14:38,967
Alice: WHAT? I DIDN’T HEAR YOU.

326
00:14:38,967 --> 00:14:40,387
Kirito: UH, NEVER MIND.

327
00:14:40,387 --> 00:14:41,557
( breeze blowing )

328
00:14:41,557 --> 00:14:42,887
Eugeo: SHH.

329
00:14:42,887 --> 00:14:44,307
- Kirito: EH?
- ( Alice gasps )

330
00:14:46,647 --> 00:14:48,397
( shudders )

331
00:14:48,397 --> 00:14:49,607
IS THAT THE WIND?

332
00:14:49,607 --> 00:14:51,687
Eugeo: YOU PICKED
THE RIGHT PATH!

333
00:14:51,687 --> 00:14:53,607
WE’RE ALMOST TO THE ENTRANCE!

334
00:14:53,607 --> 00:14:55,487
Alice: WAIT! BE CAREFUL,

335
00:14:55,487 --> 00:14:57,237
OR YOU’LL TRIP
AND HURT YOURSELF!

336
00:15:06,417 --> 00:15:07,787
Eugeo: THERE IT IS!

337
00:15:13,047 --> 00:15:14,877
♪

338
00:15:22,137 --> 00:15:24,597
( Kirito sighs ) WHERE ARE WE?

339
00:15:24,597 --> 00:15:27,767
Alice: THE DARK TERRITORY.

340
00:15:30,357 --> 00:15:32,937
Eugeo: OH, NO.
W-WE BETTER TURN AROUND.

341
00:15:32,937 --> 00:15:34,437
- ( metal clashes )
- ( kids gasp )

342
00:15:34,437 --> 00:15:36,237
♪

343
00:15:44,657 --> 00:15:46,037
Alice: DRAGON KNIGHTS.

344
00:15:46,037 --> 00:15:47,917
Kirito: THAT WHITE ONE,

345
00:15:47,917 --> 00:15:51,537
THAT’S A REAL, LIVE
INTEGRITY KNIGHT, ISN’T IT?

346
00:15:51,537 --> 00:15:54,877
Eugeo: UH-HUH, AND THE OTHER’S
FROM THE DARK TERRITORY.

347
00:16:23,577 --> 00:16:25,157
( Kirito gasps )

348
00:16:26,407 --> 00:16:27,327
( kids gasp )

349
00:16:38,167 --> 00:16:41,137
♪

350
00:16:41,137 --> 00:16:42,467
( Alice shudders )

351
00:16:56,777 --> 00:16:57,687
Kirito: NO, WAIT!

352
00:17:11,537 --> 00:17:12,537
Eugeo: ALICE!

353
00:17:12,537 --> 00:17:14,087
( boys gasp )

354
00:17:16,547 --> 00:17:18,047
( Alice gasps )

355
00:17:24,007 --> 00:17:26,927
( memory ) IN BOOK ONE,
CHAPTER THREE, VERSE 11,

356
00:17:26,927 --> 00:17:29,887
THE INDEX SAYS, "NONE SHALL
CROSS THE END MOUNTAINS

357
00:17:29,887 --> 00:17:31,477
THAT SURROUND
THE HUMAN EMPIRE."

358
00:17:31,477 --> 00:17:34,187
( Kirito gasps )

359
00:17:34,187 --> 00:17:35,357
ALICE!

360
00:17:37,977 --> 00:17:39,647
( Alice gasps )
WHAT HAVE I DONE?

361
00:17:39,647 --> 00:17:41,777
Eugeo: DON’T WORRY, ALICE.
IT’S OKAY.

362
00:17:41,777 --> 00:17:43,907
I MEAN, IT’S NOT LIKE
YOU LEFT THE CAVE.

363
00:17:43,907 --> 00:17:46,737
YOU DIDN’T.
SHE DIDN’T, DID SHE?

364
00:17:46,737 --> 00:17:48,327
KIRITO?

365
00:17:51,157 --> 00:17:53,617
( humming )

366
00:17:53,617 --> 00:17:55,327
( boys gasp )

367
00:17:55,327 --> 00:17:56,667
Eugeo: WHAT’S THAT?

368
00:17:56,667 --> 00:17:58,877
Stranger: A SINGULAR UNIT
HAS BEEN DETECTED.

369
00:17:58,877 --> 00:18:00,547
TRACING ITS I.D.

370
00:18:00,547 --> 00:18:02,507
COORDINATES FIXED.

371
00:18:02,507 --> 00:18:05,087
REPORT COMPLETE.

372
00:18:08,177 --> 00:18:10,307
Eugeo: WH-WHAT WAS THAT THING?

373
00:18:10,307 --> 00:18:11,517
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW.

374
00:18:11,517 --> 00:18:13,137
LET’S GET OUT OF HERE!

375
00:18:16,647 --> 00:18:18,317
( kids panting )

376
00:18:31,247 --> 00:18:33,247
Kirito: SO, GUYS...

377
00:18:33,247 --> 00:18:34,787
WHERE ARE WE GONNA PUT THIS?

378
00:18:36,497 --> 00:18:37,587
( Alice chuckles )

379
00:18:37,587 --> 00:18:39,997
I’LL PUT THE ICE IN MY BASEMENT,

380
00:18:39,997 --> 00:18:41,417
WHERE IT’S NICE AND COOL.

381
00:18:41,417 --> 00:18:42,587
Eugeo: O-OKAY.

382
00:18:42,587 --> 00:18:43,337
Kirito: SEE YA.

383
00:18:48,217 --> 00:18:49,307
EH?

384
00:18:50,967 --> 00:18:52,517
Alice: I THINK TOMORROW’S LUNCH

385
00:18:52,517 --> 00:18:53,887
WILL BE THE BEST ONE YET.

386
00:18:53,887 --> 00:18:55,437
Kirito: CAN’T WAIT!

387
00:18:55,437 --> 00:18:56,727
Eugeo: M-ME NEITHER.

388
00:18:56,727 --> 00:18:58,307
( Alice giggles )

389
00:19:04,357 --> 00:19:07,277
♪

390
00:19:07,277 --> 00:19:09,117
( Eugeo gasping )

391
00:19:13,697 --> 00:19:15,407
( whimpers )

392
00:19:15,407 --> 00:19:17,997
( stranger growls )

393
00:19:19,877 --> 00:19:21,167
Eugeo: ALICE.

394
00:19:26,507 --> 00:19:29,097
DON’T GO! ALICE!

395
00:19:30,507 --> 00:19:32,347
ALICE!

396
00:19:33,467 --> 00:19:34,727
( gasps )

397
00:19:34,727 --> 00:19:37,307
( insects chirping )

398
00:19:44,527 --> 00:19:45,607
( sighs )

399
00:19:45,607 --> 00:19:47,487
( ax chops )

400
00:19:49,697 --> 00:19:51,577
( Kirito exhales )

401
00:19:58,667 --> 00:20:00,787
( ax chops )

402
00:20:00,787 --> 00:20:01,707
( Eugeo gasps )

403
00:20:04,337 --> 00:20:05,257
( gasps )

404
00:20:07,337 --> 00:20:09,507
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT!

405
00:20:09,507 --> 00:20:11,847
Kirito: YEAH. HE’S THE SAME ONE
FROM YESTERDAY.

406
00:20:13,507 --> 00:20:15,977
OH, NO. ALICE.

407
00:20:15,977 --> 00:20:18,307
Eugeo: HE’S COME FOR HER.

408
00:20:18,307 --> 00:20:20,857
BUT HE CAN’T
TAKE HER AWAY FOR THAT!

409
00:20:22,397 --> 00:20:23,477
Kirito: COME ON!

410
00:20:24,897 --> 00:20:26,107
Eugeo: W-WAIT!

411
00:20:32,487 --> 00:20:34,327
( townsfolk murmuring )

412
00:20:43,997 --> 00:20:44,917
Eugeo: ALICE.

413
00:20:46,047 --> 00:20:47,967
Alice: KIRITO. EUGEO.

414
00:20:47,967 --> 00:20:50,377
Kirito: KEEP IT DOWN.

415
00:20:50,377 --> 00:20:53,347
BETTER GET OUTTA HERE
BEFORE HE SEES YOU.

416
00:20:53,347 --> 00:20:55,597
( townsfolk gasping )

417
00:20:58,427 --> 00:21:00,267
Alice: IT’S MY FATHER.

418
00:21:05,607 --> 00:21:09,447
Gasfut: I AM GASFUT ZUBERG.
THE ELDER OF THIS VILLAGE.

419
00:21:12,277 --> 00:21:14,577
Deusolbert: I AM
DEUSOLBERT SYNTHESIS SEVEN,

420
00:21:14,577 --> 00:21:15,987
THE AXIOM INTEGRITY KNIGHT

421
00:21:15,987 --> 00:21:18,997
WHO OVERSEES THE NORTHERN
NORLANGARTH TERRITORY.

422
00:21:18,997 --> 00:21:22,957
YOUR DAUGHTER, ALICE ZUBERG,
HAS DISOBEYED THE TABOO INDEX.

423
00:21:22,957 --> 00:21:24,877
I SHALL TAKE HER WITH ME

424
00:21:24,877 --> 00:21:27,957
TO ANSWER FOR HER CRIMES
AND BE EXECUTED.

425
00:21:27,957 --> 00:21:29,717
( townsfolk murmuring )

426
00:21:29,717 --> 00:21:32,927
( all gasping )

427
00:21:32,927 --> 00:21:35,427
Deusolbert: TABOO INDEX,
BOOK ONE, CHAPTER THREE,

428
00:21:35,427 --> 00:21:40,097
VERSE 11 STATES NONE SHALL
CROSS INTO THE DARK TERRITORY.

429
00:21:40,097 --> 00:21:42,437
♪

430
00:21:55,657 --> 00:21:58,237
( Alice whimpering )

431
00:22:01,117 --> 00:22:02,037
Kirito: SIR KNIGHT!

432
00:22:03,827 --> 00:22:07,337
A-ALICE NEVER SET FOOT
IN THE DARK TERRITORY!

433
00:22:07,337 --> 00:22:10,837
IT WAS AN ACCIDENT! ALL SHE DID
WAS TOUCH THE GROUND!

434
00:22:10,837 --> 00:22:13,087
IT WAS ONLY FOR A SECOND!

435
00:22:13,087 --> 00:22:15,927
Deusolbert: THAT IS ENOUGH
TO CHARGE HER WITH THE CRIME.

436
00:22:15,927 --> 00:22:19,097
Kirito: THEN WE’RE
JUST AS GUILTY AS SHE IS!

437
00:22:19,097 --> 00:22:21,017
WE WERE RIGHT THERE WITH HER!

438
00:22:21,017 --> 00:22:23,977
IF YOU TAKE HER
THEN TAKE US, TOO!

439
00:22:26,767 --> 00:22:28,767
EUGEO, LISTEN.

440
00:22:28,767 --> 00:22:31,937
I’M GONNA CHARGE HIM
WITH THE AX.

441
00:22:31,937 --> 00:22:33,107
GRAB ALICE, AND RUN.

442
00:22:33,107 --> 00:22:34,907
Eugeo: H-HOLD ON.

443
00:22:34,907 --> 00:22:36,317
I DON’T--WE CAN’T--

444
00:22:36,317 --> 00:22:37,947
Kirito: I DON’T CARE
WHAT HAPPENS.

445
00:22:37,947 --> 00:22:41,537
HER LIFE’S MORE IMPORTANT
THAN SOME STUPID OLD RULES!

446
00:22:41,537 --> 00:22:43,207
( Eugeo stammering )

447
00:22:44,617 --> 00:22:46,287
♪

448
00:23:01,557 --> 00:23:03,227
KIRITO!

449
00:23:03,227 --> 00:23:06,397
Deusolbert: ESCORT THOSE
TWO CHILDREN FROM THE SQUARE.

450
00:23:07,767 --> 00:23:08,937
Kirito: LET HER GO!

451
00:23:18,737 --> 00:23:20,657
DON’T JUST STAND THERE!
GO HELP HER!

452
00:23:31,047 --> 00:23:32,627
( Eugeo grunts )

453
00:23:32,627 --> 00:23:34,507
( gasping )

454
00:23:36,837 --> 00:23:40,547
( gasping )

455
00:23:40,547 --> 00:23:43,137
Kirito: EUGEO!
GET THESE GUYS OFF ME!

456
00:23:43,137 --> 00:23:44,767
COME ON! HURRY!

457
00:23:44,767 --> 00:23:45,517
EUGEO!

458
00:23:48,597 --> 00:23:50,437
( Eugeo stammering )

459
00:24:03,987 --> 00:24:06,707
( Kirito grunts )

460
00:24:13,747 --> 00:24:16,217
ALICE!

461
00:24:16,217 --> 00:24:17,797
( gasps )

462
00:24:17,797 --> 00:24:19,047
( sighs )

463
00:24:22,137 --> 00:24:24,057
( sighing )

464
00:24:43,657 --> 00:24:45,617
( Sinon panting )

465
00:24:45,617 --> 00:24:47,907
♪

466
00:25:17,737 --> 00:25:19,187
( trigger clicking )

467
00:25:21,607 --> 00:25:22,607
( player gasps )

468
00:25:27,237 --> 00:25:28,247
( Sinon chuckles )

469
00:25:28,247 --> 00:25:30,077
♪

470
00:25:37,547 --> 00:25:39,127
Klein: THIS TANEGASHIMA’S
FULL-AUTO!

471
00:25:43,257 --> 00:25:45,637
Lisbeth: WHAT’S UP,
YOU P.K. JERKS?

472
00:25:45,637 --> 00:25:47,557
LET’S SEE HOW FAST YOU RUN.

473
00:25:56,017 --> 00:25:58,107
( Silica laughing )

474
00:26:04,027 --> 00:26:05,197
Klein: COWARDS!

475
00:26:08,287 --> 00:26:09,697
Sinon: YOU’RE UP! I’LL COVER!

476
00:26:13,327 --> 00:26:14,247
( photon sword hums )

477
00:26:17,037 --> 00:26:19,297
♪

478
00:26:38,817 --> 00:26:40,977
Player #2:
ARE THOSE PHOTON SWORDS?

479
00:26:40,977 --> 00:26:45,407
Player #3: TEAM A NEEDS BACKUP.
B AND C, HEAD TO GRID FOUR-SIX.

480
00:26:45,407 --> 00:26:47,777
YOU HAVE PERMISSION
TO USE GRENADES.

481
00:26:47,777 --> 00:26:50,537
Player #2: HEY, BOSS,
LET ME IN ON THIS.

482
00:26:50,537 --> 00:26:52,247
Player #3: NO.
THIS OP’S ABOUT TO WIND DOWN.

483
00:26:53,367 --> 00:26:55,457
JUST SIT BACK, AND WATCH.

484
00:26:59,797 --> 00:27:00,797
( Kirito gasps )

485
00:27:09,927 --> 00:27:11,267
( chuckles )

486
00:27:17,767 --> 00:27:19,187
Asuna: I GOT THIS!

487
00:27:25,067 --> 00:27:27,237
( Kirito yells )

488
00:27:40,167 --> 00:27:41,247
( photon sword hums )

489
00:27:43,337 --> 00:27:44,967
Kirito: DAMN IT.

490
00:27:47,127 --> 00:27:48,547
( device chirps )

491
00:27:48,547 --> 00:27:51,927
Player #3:
WELL, THAT’S THE END OF THAT.

492
00:27:51,927 --> 00:27:53,517
ALL TEAMS, RETREAT.

493
00:27:53,517 --> 00:27:55,847
GRID ONE-NINE’S TOO HOT.

494
00:27:58,437 --> 00:28:00,147
Player #2: AW, WE COULD
HAVE KILLED ’EM ALL

495
00:28:00,147 --> 00:28:01,517
IF WE STUCK WITH IT.

496
00:28:01,517 --> 00:28:04,857
YOU SURE YOU WANNA
END THE DAY LIKE THIS, BOSS?

497
00:28:04,857 --> 00:28:07,447
Player #3: THAT TEAM’S
ALL OVER THE PLACE.

498
00:28:07,447 --> 00:28:10,067
FIGHTING THEM
WON’T HELP WITH OUR TRAINING.

499
00:28:10,067 --> 00:28:13,907
WE HAVE A BIG MISSION COMING UP,
AND WE NEED TO STAY SHARP.

500
00:28:13,907 --> 00:28:14,947
LET’S GO.

501
00:28:19,877 --> 00:28:22,207
Player #2: ’TIL NEXT TIME, KID.

502
00:28:26,667 --> 00:28:30,337
Klein: OH, MAN, I HEARD "G.G.O."
WAS GONNA BE HARD-CORE,

503
00:28:30,337 --> 00:28:32,257
BUT THAT WAS INSANE!

504
00:28:32,257 --> 00:28:33,677
I NEVER PLAYED A GAME

505
00:28:33,677 --> 00:28:35,597
WHERE IT’S COOL
JUST TO RUN AROUND AND KILL.

506
00:28:35,597 --> 00:28:40,017
Sinon: ACTUALLY THERE’S A METHOD
TO THE MADNESS OF P.K.ing HERE.

507
00:28:40,017 --> 00:28:42,397
YOU GO AFTER OTHER PLAYERS
FOR THEIR CASH OR ITEMS.

508
00:28:42,397 --> 00:28:45,857
BUT THE TEAM WE JUST FOUGHT
DIDN’T CARE ABOUT THAT STUFF.

509
00:28:45,857 --> 00:28:47,987
Kirito: YEAH, THE ONLY THING
THOSE GUYS WANTED

510
00:28:47,987 --> 00:28:49,607
WAS TO STRAIGHT-UP KILL US.

511
00:28:49,607 --> 00:28:52,987
AND DID YOU SEE ALL THE GRENADES
AND SMOKE BOMBS THEY USED?

512
00:28:52,987 --> 00:28:54,237
ISN’T THAT STUFF EXPENSIVE?

513
00:28:54,237 --> 00:28:56,197
Sinon: YOU KNOW IT.

514
00:28:56,197 --> 00:28:59,207
AND THAT’S HOW THEY FIGHT
EVERY SINGLE TIME THEY SHOW UP.

515
00:28:59,207 --> 00:29:02,037
THEY GO AFTER TEAMS THAT ARE
OUT IN THE MIDDLE OF NOWHERE,

516
00:29:02,037 --> 00:29:03,337
MASSACRE EVERYONE,

517
00:29:03,337 --> 00:29:06,047
THEN DISAPPEAR
WITHOUT LOOTING ANYONE.

518
00:29:06,047 --> 00:29:07,627
Asuna: I SAW THEIR STATS.

519
00:29:07,627 --> 00:29:09,417
IS IT TRUE THEY’VE
NEVER LOST A BATTLE?

520
00:29:09,417 --> 00:29:11,087
Sinon: YEAH, IT’S TRUE.
THEY HAVEN’T.

521
00:29:11,087 --> 00:29:12,797
STILL...

522
00:29:12,797 --> 00:29:15,467
I THOUGHT IF ANYONE
COULD BEAT ’EM, WE COULD,

523
00:29:15,467 --> 00:29:17,387
’CAUSE AS A TEAM,

524
00:29:17,387 --> 00:29:19,727
WE’RE NOT LIKE ANYONE
THEY’VE COME UP AGAINST YET.

525
00:29:19,727 --> 00:29:23,187
OH, WELL. I GUESS
IT JUST WASN’T IN THE CARDS.

526
00:29:23,187 --> 00:29:25,647
I DIDN’T EXPECT THEY’D RETREAT.
THAT’S FOR SURE.

527
00:29:25,647 --> 00:29:28,357
Klein: HEY, NO BIGGIE.
IT’S NOT LIKE WE LOST.

528
00:29:28,357 --> 00:29:31,447
BESIDES, THEY RAN,
SO THAT’S A WIN IN MY BOOK.

529
00:29:31,447 --> 00:29:33,567
Lisbeth: THE POINT WAS
TO FIND OUT WHO THEY WERE

530
00:29:33,567 --> 00:29:36,447
AND WHAT THEY WERE
UP TO, TOUGH GUY.

531
00:29:36,447 --> 00:29:39,157
Klein: YEAH, WELL,
A WIN’S A WIN.

532
00:29:39,157 --> 00:29:41,667
Asuna: THAT SAID,
IT WOULD HAVE BEEN NICE

533
00:29:41,667 --> 00:29:43,377
TO FIND OUT THE LEADER’S NAME.

534
00:29:43,377 --> 00:29:45,417
Silica: YEAH, BUT WITH
THE WAY THEY FOUGHT,

535
00:29:45,417 --> 00:29:47,587
IT WASN’T EVEN CLEAR
WHO THE LEADER WAS.

536
00:29:47,587 --> 00:29:48,877
( Lisbeth yelps )

537
00:29:48,877 --> 00:29:50,297
HEY, DON’T FLOP ON ME!

538
00:29:50,297 --> 00:29:52,127
WHAT DO I LOOK LIKE, A PILLOW?

539
00:29:52,127 --> 00:29:54,427
Asuna: HE SAID HE’S BEEN
TAKING TIME OFF FROM SCHOOL

540
00:29:54,427 --> 00:29:56,757
SINCE THURSDAY
AND TOURING COMPANIES.

541
00:29:56,757 --> 00:29:58,637
Sinon: KNOWING HIM,
HE’S PROBABLY MIXED UP

542
00:29:58,637 --> 00:30:00,307
IN SOMETHING SINISTER AGAIN.

543
00:30:00,307 --> 00:30:02,517
( Kirito sighing )

544
00:30:02,517 --> 00:30:06,567
Sinon: THANKS AGAIN FOR HELPING
ME OUT, GUYS. YOU’RE THE BEST.

545
00:30:06,567 --> 00:30:08,227
Klein: NO PROBS. ANYTIME!

546
00:30:08,227 --> 00:30:09,567
LATER.

547
00:30:09,567 --> 00:30:11,357
Silica: TODAY WAS FUN!

548
00:30:11,357 --> 00:30:13,067
Lisbeth: SEE YA!

549
00:30:13,067 --> 00:30:15,157
Asuna: WELL, BYE.

550
00:30:15,157 --> 00:30:17,737
- Sinon: NO, WAIT. ONE SEC.
- Asuna: WHAT’S UP?

551
00:30:17,737 --> 00:30:19,947
Sinon: I WAS HOPING YOU GUYS
COULD HELP ME WITH SOMETHING.

552
00:30:19,947 --> 00:30:22,207
Asuna: THAT SQUAD OF P.K.ers?

553
00:30:22,207 --> 00:30:25,287
Sinon: NO,
IT’S SOMETHING ELSE, ACTUALLY.

554
00:30:27,787 --> 00:30:31,337
IF YOU AND KIRITO HAVE TIME,
COULD WE MEET I.R.L. TOMORROW?

555
00:30:31,337 --> 00:30:33,427
Asuna: I THINK SO.

556
00:30:33,427 --> 00:30:35,547
YEAH, I’M FREE IN THE EVENING.

557
00:30:35,547 --> 00:30:37,097
DO YOU WANT TO MEET AT AGIL’S?

558
00:30:37,097 --> 00:30:38,307
Sinon: SURE.

559
00:30:38,307 --> 00:30:40,967
OH, I’LL ALSO
EMAIL YOU THE PLAN

560
00:30:40,967 --> 00:30:43,187
SO YOU CAN THINK ABOUT IT,
IF THAT’S OKAY.

561
00:30:43,187 --> 00:30:44,687
Asuna: SOUNDS GOOD.

562
00:30:47,517 --> 00:30:48,767
( Kirito gasps )

563
00:30:51,317 --> 00:30:54,107
Sinon: YOU’RE SO THIN.
ARE YOU EATING?

564
00:30:54,107 --> 00:30:56,407
Kirito: WHAT ARE YOU, MY MOM?

565
00:30:56,407 --> 00:31:00,157
ANYWAY, WHAT IS IT
YOU WANTED TO ASK ME?

566
00:31:00,157 --> 00:31:01,447
IS IT ABOUT B.o.B.?

567
00:31:01,447 --> 00:31:03,157
Sinon: MM-HMM.

568
00:31:03,157 --> 00:31:05,537
THERE’S A PLAYER
CALLING HIMSELF SUBTILIZER,

569
00:31:05,537 --> 00:31:07,417
WHO WON B.o.B. FOUR.

570
00:31:07,417 --> 00:31:10,497
HE’S THE SAME GUY
WHO WON THE FIRST B.o.B.

571
00:31:10,497 --> 00:31:12,087
Kirito: HUH.

572
00:31:12,087 --> 00:31:14,547
Sinon: WHEN WE FOUND OUT
HE WAS IN FOUR,

573
00:31:14,547 --> 00:31:17,637
EVERYONE GOT EXCITED, ’CAUSE
HE’S LIKE A LEGEND, YOU KNOW?

574
00:31:17,637 --> 00:31:20,307
Kirito: YEAH. WE ALL
WATCHED THE LIVE FEED.

575
00:31:20,307 --> 00:31:23,097
CAN’T BELIEVE HE STARTED
WITH JUST HIS BARE HANDS.

576
00:31:23,097 --> 00:31:25,597
HE FOUGHT WITH A CONFIDANT,
STEALTHY STYLE,

577
00:31:25,597 --> 00:31:27,307
LIKE THAT TEAM
FROM THE OTHER DAY.

578
00:31:27,307 --> 00:31:29,767
Sinon: THEY DID HAVE
THE SAME VIBE, DIDN’T THEY?

579
00:31:29,767 --> 00:31:34,277
WELL, EXCEPT SUBTILIZER’S ON
A WHOLE ’NOTHER LEVEL THAN THEM.

580
00:31:34,277 --> 00:31:35,607
( sighs )

581
00:31:35,607 --> 00:31:37,737
HE KILLED ME SO FAST.

582
00:31:37,737 --> 00:31:39,867
I DIDN’T EVEN HAVE TIME TO AIM.

583
00:31:39,867 --> 00:31:42,537
THAT’S HOW IT WAS
FOR EVERYONE IN THE TOURNEY.

584
00:31:42,537 --> 00:31:45,207
IT’S LIKE HE KNEW OUR MOVES
BEFORE WE DID.

585
00:31:45,207 --> 00:31:46,707
Kirito: NO WAY. REALLY?

586
00:31:46,707 --> 00:31:48,827
BUT YOU’RE ALL VETS AT B.o.B.

587
00:31:48,827 --> 00:31:52,167
HOW COULD HE ANTICIPATE
EVERYONE’S MOVES LIKE THAT?

588
00:31:52,167 --> 00:31:53,507
Sinon: I SUPPOSE, AS VETS,

589
00:31:53,507 --> 00:31:55,717
THERE’S A PREDICTABILITY
TO HOW WE PLAY.

590
00:31:55,717 --> 00:31:58,927
WE TEND TO USE THE SAME MOVES,
’CAUSE THEY WORK.

591
00:31:58,927 --> 00:32:01,347
WHICH BRINGS ME
TO WHY YOU’RE HERE.

592
00:32:01,347 --> 00:32:02,887
( Kirito sighs )

593
00:32:02,887 --> 00:32:04,677
Sinon: I WAS THINKING
THAT A PLAYER

594
00:32:04,677 --> 00:32:06,637
WITH A MORE CHAOTIC
FIGHTING STYLE

595
00:32:06,637 --> 00:32:09,767
MIGHT HAVE A BETTER CHANCE
AT OUTMANEUVERING SUBTILIZER.

596
00:32:09,767 --> 00:32:12,477
ANYWAY, THE POINT
IS THE NEXT B.o.B.’S

597
00:32:12,477 --> 00:32:14,357
GONNA BE HAPPENING
AT THE END OF THE YEAR,

598
00:32:14,357 --> 00:32:16,527
AND I’D LIKE YOU
TO SIGN UP FOR IT.

599
00:32:16,527 --> 00:32:18,357
Kirito: HUH? UH...

600
00:32:18,357 --> 00:32:20,487
Sinon: THERE’S NO WAY
I’M GONNA LET MYSELF LOSE

601
00:32:20,487 --> 00:32:23,027
TO THE SAME GUY AGAIN.
HE’S GOING DOWN.

602
00:32:24,657 --> 00:32:26,747
Kirito: LOOKS LIKE
YOU MADE SOME PROGRESS.

603
00:32:26,747 --> 00:32:29,367
Sinon: O-OH, YEAH.

604
00:32:29,367 --> 00:32:31,627
I STILL GET THE SHAKES
EVERY NOW AND THEN,

605
00:32:31,627 --> 00:32:33,297
BUT I’M GETTING BETTER.

606
00:32:34,667 --> 00:32:35,757
Kirito: AND YOUR FRIEND,

607
00:32:35,757 --> 00:32:37,507
IS HE DOING ANY BETTER?

608
00:32:37,507 --> 00:32:38,507
( Sinon sighs )

609
00:32:38,507 --> 00:32:40,837
YOU MEAN SHINKAWA.

610
00:32:40,837 --> 00:32:43,967
YEAH, HE’S MAKING PROGRESS.

611
00:32:43,967 --> 00:32:47,727
I’LL PROBABLY GO VISIT HIM
AGAIN IN A COUPLE DAYS.

612
00:32:47,727 --> 00:32:49,347
Kirito: THAT’S GOOD.

613
00:32:49,347 --> 00:32:51,607
WELL, LOOK ON THE BRIGHT SIDE.

614
00:32:51,607 --> 00:32:54,687
HE’S FINALLY GETTING THE HELP
HE NEEDS. DEATH GUN’S OVER.

615
00:32:54,687 --> 00:32:56,357
Sinon: NO, IT ISN’T.

616
00:32:56,357 --> 00:32:58,397
HIS PARTNER’S
STILL OUT THERE, REMEMBER?

617
00:32:58,397 --> 00:33:01,317
Kirito: YEAH, BUT KIKUOKA SAID

618
00:33:01,317 --> 00:33:02,737
THEY’LL CATCH UP WITH HIM
SOON ENOUGH.

619
00:33:02,737 --> 00:33:04,907
Sinon: YEAH, I HOPE SO.

620
00:33:04,907 --> 00:33:07,747
- ( entry bell rings )
- Asuna: WHEW. SORRY I’M LATE!

621
00:33:07,747 --> 00:33:09,287
HEY THERE, SHINONON!

622
00:33:09,287 --> 00:33:10,617
Kirito: WHAT’D YOU
JUST CALL HER?

623
00:33:10,617 --> 00:33:12,997
Sinon: HEY, ASUNA.
RIGHT ON TIME.

624
00:33:12,997 --> 00:33:16,707
Asuna: I READ YOUR EMAIL
ABOUT B.o.B. FIVE. I’M IN.

625
00:33:16,707 --> 00:33:19,047
Kirito: WAIT.
YOU ASKED HER TO HELP, TOO?

626
00:33:19,047 --> 00:33:21,257
Sinon: YUP. I FIGURED
IF IT WERE JUST YOU,

627
00:33:21,257 --> 00:33:23,427
THERE’S A CHANCE
YOU’D GET TOO AGGRO.

628
00:33:23,427 --> 00:33:25,637
EVEN GOOD DOGS
NEED A LEASH, RIGHT?

629
00:33:25,637 --> 00:33:26,637
Kirito: DANG.

630
00:33:26,637 --> 00:33:29,097
Asuna: HEY, KIRITO.

631
00:33:29,097 --> 00:33:32,267
YOU’RE SO THIN. ARE YOU EATING?

632
00:33:32,267 --> 00:33:33,647
Kirito: YEAH, I AM.

633
00:33:33,647 --> 00:33:35,107
Sinon: HAH! SEE?

634
00:33:35,107 --> 00:33:37,397
SHE CAN EVEN TELL
SOMETHING’S UP.

635
00:33:37,397 --> 00:33:38,737
Asuna: IT’S THAT PART-TIME JOB,
ISN’T IT?

636
00:33:38,737 --> 00:33:40,567
HONESTLY.

637
00:33:40,567 --> 00:33:41,857
Kirito: UH...

638
00:33:41,857 --> 00:33:44,697
Asuna: PHYSICALLY,
YOU’RE FINE, SO FAR.

639
00:33:44,697 --> 00:33:46,787
Sinon: WAIT. YOU CAN TELL?

640
00:33:46,787 --> 00:33:47,827
EH?

641
00:33:47,827 --> 00:33:50,367
WHAT’S THAT?

642
00:33:50,367 --> 00:33:52,537
Kirito: IT’S EXACTLY
WHAT IT LOOKS LIKE.

643
00:33:52,537 --> 00:33:55,537
Sinon: HUH?! YOU MEAN
SHE CAN TRACK YOUR VITALS?!

644
00:33:55,537 --> 00:33:57,167
Asuna: NEAT, HUH?

645
00:33:57,167 --> 00:33:58,457
Sinon: YEAH, I GUESS,

646
00:33:58,457 --> 00:34:00,257
BUT, LIKE, HOW’S IT WORK?

647
00:34:00,257 --> 00:34:01,757
Kirito: A LITTLE WHILE AGO,

648
00:34:01,757 --> 00:34:05,257
I HAD THIS MINIATURE SENSOR
IMPLANTED IN MY CHEST.

649
00:34:05,257 --> 00:34:07,757
IT SENDS MY HEART RATE,
BODY TEMPERATURE,

650
00:34:07,757 --> 00:34:10,227
AND OTHER STUFF OVER THE NET
TO ASUNA’S SMARTPHONE.

651
00:34:10,227 --> 00:34:12,977
Sinon: WHAT?!
WH-WHY WOULD YOU WANNA DO--

652
00:34:12,977 --> 00:34:16,057
OH, I GET IT.
IT’S AN ANTI-CHEATING SYSTEM.

653
00:34:16,057 --> 00:34:18,357
- Kirito: NO! NOT EVEN!
- Asuna: NO! NOT EVEN!

654
00:34:18,357 --> 00:34:20,357
Kirito: WHEN I STARTED
THIS PART-TIME JOB,

655
00:34:20,357 --> 00:34:22,697
THEY THOUGHT
IT’D BE GOOD TO GET IT.

656
00:34:22,697 --> 00:34:25,407
I HAVE TO WEAR ELECTRODES,
AND STICKING ’EM ON

657
00:34:25,407 --> 00:34:27,527
AND PULLING ’EM OFF’S
KIND OF A HASSLE.

658
00:34:27,527 --> 00:34:32,037
USING IT LIKE THIS WAS HER IDEA,
SO I MADE A LITTLE APP FOR IT.

659
00:34:32,037 --> 00:34:33,787
Asuna: YEAH, SOMETHING
ABOUT LOOKING AT IT’S

660
00:34:33,787 --> 00:34:35,417
KIND OF SOOTHING,

661
00:34:35,417 --> 00:34:39,127
KNOWING THAT’S KIRITO’S HEART
BEATING. ( sighs )

662
00:34:39,127 --> 00:34:41,377
I GET ALL WOOZY,
AND MY HEAD STARTS TO SPIN.

663
00:34:41,377 --> 00:34:42,837
( Kirito sighs, chuckles )

664
00:34:42,837 --> 00:34:46,507
Sinon: UH, THAT’S BOTH CUTE
AND KINDA CREEPY.

665
00:34:46,507 --> 00:34:48,967
A-ANYWAY, WITH YOU ON MY SIDE,

666
00:34:48,967 --> 00:34:50,887
I’LL HAVE A MACHINE GUN
IN MY PILLBOX.

667
00:34:50,887 --> 00:34:53,687
YOU’RE EXACTLY THE EDGE I NEED.

668
00:34:53,687 --> 00:34:55,647
Asuna: I’M HAPPY TO HELP
ANY WAY I CAN.

669
00:34:55,647 --> 00:34:57,107
( Kirito chuckles )

670
00:34:57,107 --> 00:34:58,857
- Sinon: NOW, THEN...
- Kirito: WHAT?

671
00:34:58,857 --> 00:35:00,067
Sinon: I WANNA HEAR SOME MORE

672
00:35:00,067 --> 00:35:02,187
ABOUT THIS SKETCHY
NEW JOB OF YOURS.

673
00:35:02,187 --> 00:35:03,817
LET ME GUESS.

674
00:35:03,817 --> 00:35:07,567
YOU’RE ALPHA TESTING
A NEW V.R.M.M.O. GAME, RIGHT?

675
00:35:07,567 --> 00:35:10,037
Kirito: ACTUALLY,
IT’S NOT A GAME.

676
00:35:10,037 --> 00:35:12,657
IT’S A BRAIN-MACHINE INTERFACE

677
00:35:12,657 --> 00:35:14,997
DESIGNED FOR THIS
BRAND-NEW FULL-DIVE SYSTEM.

678
00:35:14,997 --> 00:35:18,127
RATH DEVELOPED IT.
THEY’RE NEW.

679
00:35:18,127 --> 00:35:20,497
Sinon: WHAT THE HECK
KIND OF A NAME IS "RATH"?

680
00:35:20,497 --> 00:35:22,837
Asuna: IT’S THE NAME
OF AN IMAGINARY CREATURE.

681
00:35:22,837 --> 00:35:25,587
I REMEMBER IT FROM THE BOOK
"THROUGH THE LOOKING-GLASS."

682
00:35:25,587 --> 00:35:28,757
SOME CHARACTERS SAID IT WAS
A PIG, AND OTHERS, A TURTLE.

683
00:35:28,757 --> 00:35:30,347
Sinon: SO ARE THEY RELEASING

684
00:35:30,347 --> 00:35:33,057
SOME NEXT-GEN FULL-DIVE RIG
FOR GAMING?

685
00:35:33,057 --> 00:35:36,187
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW. MAYBE.

686
00:35:36,187 --> 00:35:38,017
THIS THING’S TOTALLY DIFFERENT

687
00:35:38,017 --> 00:35:40,517
COMPARED TO THE FULL-DIVE TECH
THAT’S OUT NOW.

688
00:35:40,517 --> 00:35:43,607
Sinon: OH. SO WHAT’S
THE IN-GAME WORLD LIKE?

689
00:35:45,197 --> 00:35:48,487
- Kirito: I HAVE NO IDEA.
- Sinon: HUH?

690
00:35:48,487 --> 00:35:50,657
Kirito: IT’S HOW THEY
KEEP THINGS CONFIDENTIAL.

691
00:35:50,657 --> 00:35:54,447
THE MEMORIES I MAKE USING
THEIR RIG IN THE V.R. WORLD,

692
00:35:54,447 --> 00:35:57,167
THEY DON’T STICK WITH ME
IN THE REAL WORLD.

693
00:35:57,167 --> 00:35:59,877
WHATEVER I SAW DURING THE TESTS,
WHATEVER I DID,

694
00:35:59,877 --> 00:36:02,707
I FORGET ALL OF IT
AFTER I LOG OUT.

695
00:36:02,707 --> 00:36:04,377
- Sinon: UH, HUH?!
- ( Asuna gasps )

696
00:36:04,377 --> 00:36:06,797
Sinon: YOU CAN’T REMEMBER
ANYTHING AT ALL?

697
00:36:06,797 --> 00:36:10,047
OH, MY GOD.
IS IT ANOTHER AUGMA?

698
00:36:10,047 --> 00:36:14,097
Kirito: UH, N-NO.
IT’S NOT LIKE THAT!

699
00:36:14,097 --> 00:36:17,307
THIS RIG DOESN’T PUT STRESS ON
YOUR BRAIN LIKE THE AUGMA DID.

700
00:36:17,307 --> 00:36:19,397
I DIDN’T LOSE MY MEMORIES
OR ANYTHING.

701
00:36:19,397 --> 00:36:21,727
I JUST CAN’T ACCESS THEM
FROM MY FLUCTLIGHT.

702
00:36:21,727 --> 00:36:24,187
- Sinon: UH...
- Asuna: A FLUCT WHAT?

703
00:36:24,187 --> 00:36:27,527
Kirito: THIS IS GONNA
TAKE SOME TIME TO EXPLAIN.

704
00:36:27,527 --> 00:36:29,157
FIRST OFF,

705
00:36:29,157 --> 00:36:32,777
THE RIG I’M TESTING’S
CALLED THE SOUL TRANSLATOR.

706
00:36:34,787 --> 00:36:37,407
WHERE IN YOUR BODY
DO YOU THINK YOUR SOUL IS?

707
00:36:37,407 --> 00:36:38,787
Asuna: SERIOUSLY?

708
00:36:38,787 --> 00:36:41,127
Sinon: I DON’T KNOW.
IN THE BRAIN?

709
00:36:41,127 --> 00:36:43,127
Kirito: IF YOU ZOOM IN
TO THE BRAIN,

710
00:36:43,127 --> 00:36:45,207
YOU’LL SEE
IT’S MADE UP OF CELLS.

711
00:36:45,207 --> 00:36:49,427
SO WHERE IN ALL THOSE CELLS
DO YOU THINK THE SOUL IS?

712
00:36:49,427 --> 00:36:50,887
Sinon: I-I DON’T KNOW.

713
00:36:50,887 --> 00:36:52,347
Kirito: ZOOM IN TO A BRAIN CELL,

714
00:36:52,347 --> 00:36:54,137
AND YOU’LL SEE
THAT IT HAS THINGS IN IT

715
00:36:54,137 --> 00:36:55,927
THAT SUPPORT
THE CELL’S STRUCTURE.

716
00:36:55,927 --> 00:36:57,637
THEY’RE CALLED MICROTUBULES.

717
00:36:57,637 --> 00:36:58,887
Sinon: OKAY.

718
00:36:58,887 --> 00:37:00,807
Kirito: LIKE THE NAME IMPLIES,

719
00:37:00,807 --> 00:37:03,647
THEY’RE LIKE HOLLOW PIPES,
BUT THEY’RE NOT EMPTY.

720
00:37:03,647 --> 00:37:05,977
THEY GOT SOMETHING
SEALED INSIDE.

721
00:37:05,977 --> 00:37:08,697
Sinon: SO WHAT
DO THEY HAVE INSIDE?

722
00:37:08,697 --> 00:37:10,407
Kirito: LIGHT.

723
00:37:10,407 --> 00:37:14,157
THAT’S IT, FLUCTUATING LIGHT.

724
00:37:14,157 --> 00:37:16,657
IT’S THE BUILDING BLOCK
OF THE HUMAN SOUL,

725
00:37:16,657 --> 00:37:17,947
ACCORDING TO RATH.

726
00:37:17,947 --> 00:37:20,117
Asuna: SO LET ME SEE
IF I UNDERSTAND THIS.

727
00:37:20,117 --> 00:37:23,957
THEY’RE SAYING THIS LIGHT
IN BRAIN CELLS, THAT’S THE SOUL?

728
00:37:23,957 --> 00:37:25,667
Kirito: YEAH.

729
00:37:25,667 --> 00:37:28,087
THEY DON’T CALL IT
A SOUL AT RATH, THOUGH.

730
00:37:28,087 --> 00:37:30,127
THEY DECIDED TO GO
WITH A COMBINATION

731
00:37:30,127 --> 00:37:32,837
OF THE WORDS "FLUCTUATING"
AND "LIGHT,"

732
00:37:32,837 --> 00:37:34,797
"FLUCTLIGHT" FOR SHORT.

733
00:37:34,797 --> 00:37:35,887
Sinon: HUH.

734
00:37:35,887 --> 00:37:37,427
Asuna: THEN THE SOUL TRANSLATOR

735
00:37:37,427 --> 00:37:39,017
DOESN’T JUST READ
A PERSON’S BRAIN.

736
00:37:39,017 --> 00:37:40,767
IT READS THEIR FLUCTLIGHT.

737
00:37:40,767 --> 00:37:43,727
WHICH MEANS IT CAN
ALSO IMPRINT ON THEM.

738
00:37:43,727 --> 00:37:44,977
Sinon: IMPRINT?

739
00:37:44,977 --> 00:37:46,517
Asuna: LIKE THE AMUSPHERE.

740
00:37:46,517 --> 00:37:49,567
THAT RIG LETS YOU EXPERIENCE
V.R. BY SENDING IMAGES,

741
00:37:49,567 --> 00:37:52,817
SOUNDS, AND OTHER SENSORY
INFORMATION TO YOUR BRAIN.

742
00:37:52,817 --> 00:37:55,327
WITH THIS RIG,
SINCE IT’S NEXT-GEN AND ALL,

743
00:37:55,327 --> 00:37:58,197
IT WOULD WORK THE SAME WAY,
BUT ON YOUR SOUL, RIGHT?

744
00:37:58,197 --> 00:38:00,247
Kirito: YEAH, THAT’S RIGHT.

745
00:38:00,247 --> 00:38:02,457
THE NAME
PRETTY MUCH SAYS IT ALL.

746
00:38:02,457 --> 00:38:05,037
THE SOUL TRANSLATOR, OR S.T.L.,

747
00:38:05,037 --> 00:38:07,707
WRITES SHORT-TERM MEMORIES
ONTO YOUR FLUCTLIGHT

748
00:38:07,707 --> 00:38:10,507
OF THE SIGHTS AND SOUNDS
IT WANTS YOU TO EXPERIENCE.

749
00:38:10,507 --> 00:38:14,217
MNEMONIC VISUAL DATA
IS WHAT IT’S CALLED.

750
00:38:14,217 --> 00:38:18,427
I REMEMBER THE TEST DIVES I TOOK
AT THE BEGINNING OF THE JOB.

751
00:38:18,427 --> 00:38:19,847
( note vibrates )

752
00:38:19,847 --> 00:38:21,387
THOSE DIVES WERE DIFFERENT.

753
00:38:21,387 --> 00:38:23,687
I WAS BLOWN AWAY.

754
00:38:23,687 --> 00:38:26,107
IT’S NOTHING LIKE
WHAT THE AMUSPHERE CREATES.

755
00:38:26,107 --> 00:38:29,027
EVERYTHING WAS SO REAL,

756
00:38:29,027 --> 00:38:31,987
I COULDN’T TELL IT WAS
A VIRTUAL WORLD AT FIRST.

757
00:38:31,987 --> 00:38:34,817
Asuna: I DON’T KNOW.
THIS SCARES ME.

758
00:38:34,817 --> 00:38:38,327
I MEAN, IS IT SAFE?

759
00:38:38,327 --> 00:38:41,077
MR. KIKUOKA OFFERED YOU THE JOB,
AND THAT’S GREAT,

760
00:38:41,077 --> 00:38:42,787
BUT WHO KNOWS
WHAT HIS MOTIVES ARE?

761
00:38:42,787 --> 00:38:43,917
( Kirito sighs )

762
00:38:43,917 --> 00:38:45,667
YEAH, YOU’RE RIGHT,

763
00:38:45,667 --> 00:38:48,457
BUT I DON’T LET MY GUARD DOWN
AROUND HIM EVER.

764
00:38:48,457 --> 00:38:51,707
THE THING IS I WANNA KNOW.

765
00:38:51,707 --> 00:38:55,677
I HAVE TO DO THIS TO SEE
WHERE FULL-DIVE’S HEADING.

766
00:38:55,677 --> 00:38:59,717
I KNOW IT’S RISKY,
BUT THE S.T.L.’S SPECIAL.

767
00:38:59,717 --> 00:39:03,767
SURE TERMS LIKE "MNEMONIC"
AND "FLUCTLIGHT" SOUND CREEPY,

768
00:39:03,767 --> 00:39:05,137
BUT I CONNECT WITH IT.

769
00:39:05,137 --> 00:39:07,147
WAY MORE THAN THE AMUSPHERE.

770
00:39:07,147 --> 00:39:09,727
IT’S LIKE A WAKING DREAM
WHEN I’M IN IT.

771
00:39:09,727 --> 00:39:11,107
Asuna: HOW SO?

772
00:39:11,107 --> 00:39:13,317
Kirito: YOU KNOW
HOW YOU SOMETIMES HAVE DREAMS

773
00:39:13,317 --> 00:39:15,907
THAT SEEM LONG,
THE KIND WHERE YOU WAKE UP

774
00:39:15,907 --> 00:39:18,407
AND YOU’D SWEAR THAT DREAM
WENT ON FOR HOURS,

775
00:39:18,407 --> 00:39:20,947
ESPECIALLY IF IT
WAS A NIGHTMARE?

776
00:39:20,947 --> 00:39:22,747
THE TRUTH IS, THAT DREAM

777
00:39:22,747 --> 00:39:24,787
PROBABLY ONLY LASTED
A FEW MINUTES.

778
00:39:24,787 --> 00:39:28,587
YOU GET THAT SAME PHENOMENA
IF YOU DIVE WITH THE S.T.L.

779
00:39:28,587 --> 00:39:29,747
Sinon: SERIOUSLY?

780
00:39:29,747 --> 00:39:31,667
Kirito: IT’S JUST LIKE A DREAM

781
00:39:31,667 --> 00:39:34,717
THAT FELT LIKE HOURS,
BUT WAS ONLY A FEW MINUTES.

782
00:39:34,717 --> 00:39:38,467
YOUR TIME DIVING WITH THE S.T.L.
IS WAY LONGER THAN YOUR DIVE.

783
00:39:38,467 --> 00:39:40,177
( Sinon gasps )

784
00:39:40,177 --> 00:39:42,427
Kirito: THAT’S THE MAIN FEATURE
OF THE S.T.L.

785
00:39:42,427 --> 00:39:44,887
RATH CALLS IT
FLUCTLIGHT ACCELERATION,

786
00:39:44,887 --> 00:39:48,147
OR F.L.A. FOR SHORT.

787
00:39:48,147 --> 00:39:49,647
Sinon: WHOA.

788
00:39:49,647 --> 00:39:51,147
Asuna: I’M SO CONFUSED.

789
00:39:51,147 --> 00:39:52,647
Sinon: MY HEAD’S SPINNING.

790
00:39:52,647 --> 00:39:55,447
YOU WERE DIVING
FOR THREE WHOLE DAYS,

791
00:39:55,447 --> 00:39:57,947
SO HOW MUCH TIME
WAS THAT IN V.R.?

792
00:39:57,947 --> 00:39:59,487
Kirito: MM, I’M NOT SURE.

793
00:39:59,487 --> 00:40:02,037
IT COULD HAVE BEEN TEN DAYS
OR A MONTH.

794
00:40:02,037 --> 00:40:04,197
I DON’T REMEMBER HOW LONG.

795
00:40:04,197 --> 00:40:07,417
WHEN I ASKED HOW LONG,
THEY WOULDN’T TELL ME,

796
00:40:07,417 --> 00:40:10,127
BUT THEY DID TELL ME
THE CODE NAME OF THE TEST WORLD.

797
00:40:10,127 --> 00:40:12,167
Sinon: REALLY? WHAT IS IT?

798
00:40:12,167 --> 00:40:13,707
Kirito: THE UNDERWORLD.

799
00:40:13,707 --> 00:40:16,127
Sinon: SO IT’S LIKE
AN UNDERGROUND WORLD?

800
00:40:16,127 --> 00:40:17,377
Asuna: IT’S A REFERENCE.

801
00:40:17,377 --> 00:40:19,927
IT HAS TO DO WITH "ALICE,"
SAME AS RATH.

802
00:40:19,927 --> 00:40:21,467
"ALICE IN WONDERLAND"
WAS THE TITLE

803
00:40:21,467 --> 00:40:23,007
THE BOOK WAS PUBLISHED UNDER,

804
00:40:23,007 --> 00:40:25,807
BUT IT HAD A DIFFERENT TITLE
WHEN IT WAS BEING WRITTEN.

805
00:40:25,807 --> 00:40:28,017
ORIGINALLY IT WAS CALLED

806
00:40:28,017 --> 00:40:29,897
"ALICE’S ADVENTURES
UNDER GROUND."

807
00:40:29,897 --> 00:40:30,977
( Kirito sighs )

808
00:40:30,977 --> 00:40:33,267
Sinon: YOU OKAY?

809
00:40:33,267 --> 00:40:35,487
Kirito: WHEN I HEARD
THE NAME "ALICE,"

810
00:40:35,487 --> 00:40:38,197
IT FELT LIKE I WAS
ABOUT TO REMEMBER SOMETHING.

811
00:40:38,197 --> 00:40:40,197
Sinon: SOMETHING ABOUT THE TEST?

812
00:40:40,197 --> 00:40:41,657
Kirito: I’M NOT SURE.

813
00:40:41,657 --> 00:40:44,867
IT FEELS LIKE
THERE’S SOMETHING I NEED TO DO.

814
00:40:44,867 --> 00:40:47,077
I JUST CAN’T REMEMBER WHAT.

815
00:40:47,077 --> 00:40:49,537
( Asuna sighs )

816
00:40:50,877 --> 00:40:51,877
Sinon: THANKS, AGIL.

817
00:40:51,877 --> 00:40:53,127
SEE YOU LATER!

818
00:40:53,127 --> 00:40:54,667
- Agil: BYE, GUYS!
- ( entry bell rings )

819
00:41:00,837 --> 00:41:03,347
Sinon: I’LL KEEP YOU GUYS
UP TO DATE ABOUT B.o.B.

820
00:41:03,347 --> 00:41:05,807
THANKS AGAIN
FOR MEETING UP WITH ME TODAY.

821
00:41:05,807 --> 00:41:07,847
Asuna: SURE!
SEE YOU LATER, SHINONON!

822
00:41:07,847 --> 00:41:08,727
Sinon: SEE YOU.

823
00:41:10,137 --> 00:41:11,647
Asuna: THAT WAS FUN.

824
00:41:11,647 --> 00:41:12,977
EH?

825
00:41:12,977 --> 00:41:14,017
WHAT’S WRONG?

826
00:41:14,017 --> 00:41:15,267
Kirito: SAY WHAT?

827
00:41:15,267 --> 00:41:17,687
OH. NOTHING.

828
00:41:17,687 --> 00:41:19,607
♪

829
00:41:25,027 --> 00:41:25,947
( sighs )

830
00:41:27,947 --> 00:41:28,907
( Asuna sighs )

831
00:41:35,037 --> 00:41:36,497
TALK TO ME.

832
00:41:39,127 --> 00:41:40,337
Kirito: ASUNA...

833
00:41:42,137 --> 00:41:45,217
I THINK I’M GONNA GO.

834
00:41:45,217 --> 00:41:47,177
- Asuna: TO AMERICA?
- Kirito: YEAH.

835
00:41:47,177 --> 00:41:50,437
THE RESEARCH IS
WAY MORE ADVANCED THERE.

836
00:41:50,437 --> 00:41:52,897
IT’S ALL NEXT-GEN STUFF.

837
00:41:52,897 --> 00:41:54,607
THEY’RE CREATING A NEW WORLD,

838
00:41:54,607 --> 00:41:58,027
AND I WANNA BE THERE
WHEN IT’S BORN.

839
00:41:58,027 --> 00:41:59,237
( Asuna chuckles )

840
00:41:59,237 --> 00:42:01,567
WE WERE HAPPY IN AINCRAD.

841
00:42:01,567 --> 00:42:04,907
BUT THERE WAS
SO MUCH PAIN AND SADNESS, TOO.

842
00:42:04,907 --> 00:42:06,277
YOU WANT TO FIND OUT

843
00:42:06,277 --> 00:42:08,577
WHY THAT CASTLE STILL
HAUNTS YOUR THOUGHTS

844
00:42:08,577 --> 00:42:11,907
AND WHERE THAT EXPERIENCE
IS TAKING YOU.

845
00:42:11,907 --> 00:42:13,997
Kirito: EVEN IF I LIVED
A COUPLE HUNDRED YEARS,

846
00:42:13,997 --> 00:42:15,997
I DOUBT I’D EVER FIND THAT OUT.

847
00:42:15,997 --> 00:42:19,587
ANYWAY, I-I WANT...

848
00:42:21,167 --> 00:42:24,137
I WANT YOU WITH ME,
ASUNA, ALWAYS.

849
00:42:24,137 --> 00:42:27,047
I WANT YOU TO COME WITH ME,

850
00:42:27,047 --> 00:42:31,097
AND I-I KNOW THAT’S ASKING
A LOT, BUT THE TRUTH IS...

851
00:42:31,097 --> 00:42:33,687
I CAN’T DO THIS WITHOUT YOU!

852
00:42:33,687 --> 00:42:34,847
( Asuna gasps )

853
00:42:34,847 --> 00:42:37,267
( sighs )

854
00:42:40,027 --> 00:42:42,737
OF COURSE.
I’LL GO ANYWHERE WITH YOU.

855
00:42:42,737 --> 00:42:46,277
IT DOESN’T MATTER WHERE.
I’LL GO.

856
00:42:46,277 --> 00:42:47,777
Kirito: ASUNA.

857
00:42:58,287 --> 00:42:59,627
( footsteps echoing )

858
00:42:59,627 --> 00:43:01,667
Asuna: SO DOES THIS MEAN
THE SOUL TRANSLATOR

859
00:43:01,667 --> 00:43:03,167
ISN’T THE NEXT STEP IN V.R.?

860
00:43:03,167 --> 00:43:06,387
HEARING YOU TALK ABOUT IT,
I THOUGHT IT WAS.

861
00:43:06,387 --> 00:43:09,507
Kirito: EH, I DON’T KNOW.

862
00:43:09,507 --> 00:43:12,677
FOR SOME REASON,
I GET THE FEELING ITS PURPOSE

863
00:43:12,677 --> 00:43:15,187
ISN’T JUST TO FULL-DIVE
IN V.R. WORLDS.

864
00:43:15,187 --> 00:43:16,807
Asuna: THEN WHAT’S IT FOR?

865
00:43:16,807 --> 00:43:18,267
Kirito: A TOOL FOR LEARNING

866
00:43:18,267 --> 00:43:20,977
ABOUT FLUCTLIGHTS
AND HUMAN CONSCIOUSNESS.

867
00:43:20,977 --> 00:43:22,277
Asuna: HMM?

868
00:43:22,277 --> 00:43:23,897
Kirito: IT’S LIKE...

869
00:43:23,897 --> 00:43:27,317
WHATEVER I KNOW ABOUT THE S.T.L.
MAKES ME THINK

870
00:43:27,317 --> 00:43:30,407
IT MIGHT BE AN EXTENSION
OF KAYABA’S IDEAS.

871
00:43:30,407 --> 00:43:33,157
( Asuna gasps )
HE’S BEHIND IT?!

872
00:43:33,157 --> 00:43:35,617
Kirito: I DON’T KNOW WHY HE
MADE THE NERVEGEAR AND "S.A.O."

873
00:43:35,617 --> 00:43:38,877
TO TRAP EVERYONE
AND MAKE US ALL SUFFER

874
00:43:38,877 --> 00:43:41,167
OR WHY HE’D FRY HIS OWN BRAIN.

875
00:43:41,167 --> 00:43:45,297
AND THE SEED, HE DIDN’T MAKE IT
JUST TO KEEP V.R. ALIVE.

876
00:43:46,757 --> 00:43:48,757
I WANNA KNOW
WHAT HIS ENDGAME WAS,

877
00:43:48,757 --> 00:43:50,427
BUT I DON’T WANT IT TO BE MINE.

878
00:43:50,427 --> 00:43:52,347
I’M NOT HIS PUPPET,

879
00:43:52,347 --> 00:43:55,097
AND IF I GO DOWN THAT ROAD,
I WOULD BE.

880
00:43:55,097 --> 00:43:56,557
Asuna: YOU SAID
YOU TALKED TO HIM

881
00:43:56,557 --> 00:43:58,727
OR THE PART OF HIM
HE LEFT BEHIND.

882
00:43:58,727 --> 00:44:00,267
Kirito: YEAH.

883
00:44:00,267 --> 00:44:03,937
I THINK I KNOW WHY HE LEFT
A COPY OF HIMSELF OUT THERE,

884
00:44:03,937 --> 00:44:05,737
AND IT MIGHT
HAVE SOMETHING TO DO

885
00:44:05,737 --> 00:44:08,357
WITH WHAT RATH’S UP TO
WITH THE S.T.L.

886
00:44:08,357 --> 00:44:09,987
- EH?
- Asuna: EH?

887
00:44:09,987 --> 00:44:12,947
Man: HEY, SORRY TO BOTHER YOU.

888
00:44:12,947 --> 00:44:16,157
I’M SORTA LOST.
WHERE’S THE STATION?

889
00:44:16,157 --> 00:44:17,957
Asuna: OH, JUST DOWN THERE.

890
00:44:19,287 --> 00:44:22,037
KIRITO?

891
00:44:22,037 --> 00:44:24,257
Kirito: YOU FOLLOWED US
FROM DICEY’S CAFE.

892
00:44:24,257 --> 00:44:25,757
( man sighs )

893
00:44:25,757 --> 00:44:28,127
THERE GOES MY PLAN
TO AMBUSH Y’ALL.

894
00:44:28,127 --> 00:44:29,257
Kirito: WHO ARE YOU?

895
00:44:29,257 --> 00:44:31,137
Man: AH, COME ON, KIRITO.

896
00:44:31,137 --> 00:44:33,137
DON’T YOU RECOGNIZE ME?

897
00:44:33,137 --> 00:44:37,887
OH. THAT’S RIGHT.
I ALWAYS WORE A MASK BACK THERE.

898
00:44:37,887 --> 00:44:40,397
YEAH, NOW THAT
XAXA’S BEEN CAUGHT,

899
00:44:40,397 --> 00:44:43,857
THERE’S NO ONE LEFT
TO FINISH THINGS BUT ME,

900
00:44:43,857 --> 00:44:46,567
THE LAST SURVIVOR
OF LAUGHING COFFIN...

901
00:44:48,067 --> 00:44:49,907
Kirito: JOHNNY BLACK!

902
00:44:51,237 --> 00:44:52,487
( gasps )

903
00:44:52,487 --> 00:44:54,867
( Johnny laughing )

904
00:44:57,197 --> 00:45:00,287
YOU ASS! YOU GOT NO SWORD HERE!

905
00:45:00,287 --> 00:45:03,127
Kirito: SO YOU’RE
STILL ON THE RUN?

906
00:45:03,127 --> 00:45:05,047
Johnny: OF COURSE!

907
00:45:05,047 --> 00:45:07,417
DAMN, KIRITO. ( laughs )

908
00:45:07,417 --> 00:45:09,297
I CAN’T BELIEVE
YOU’RE THE SAME DUDE

909
00:45:09,297 --> 00:45:11,297
THAT BEAT THE HELL OUTTA US!

910
00:45:11,297 --> 00:45:14,057
BUT YOU’RE JUST A PUNK-ASS KID,
AIN’T YOU?

911
00:45:14,057 --> 00:45:16,467
TAKE AWAY YOUR SWORDS,
AND YOU’RE NOTHING.

912
00:45:16,467 --> 00:45:17,677
Kirito: WHAT ABOUT YOU?

913
00:45:17,677 --> 00:45:19,767
YOU DON’T HAVE
YOUR POISON DAGGER.

914
00:45:21,147 --> 00:45:22,357
Johnny: I DON’T?

915
00:45:22,357 --> 00:45:25,817
YOU SURE ABOUT THAT, KIRITO?!

916
00:45:25,817 --> 00:45:27,527
Kirito: DEATH GUN.

917
00:45:27,527 --> 00:45:30,737
( Johnny laughing )

918
00:45:35,027 --> 00:45:36,787
Kirito: RUN! GET OUTTA HERE!

919
00:45:42,707 --> 00:45:44,377
- ( hypodermic hisses )
- ( Asuna gasps )

920
00:45:44,377 --> 00:45:45,997
♪

921
